From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dale Curtis <dalecurtis@chromium.org>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 17:48:14 -0700
Subject: Key media UrlIndex by requesting SecurityOrigin

Include the requesting document's SecurityOrigin in UrlData::KeyType so
that cross-origin documents sharing a renderer process (such as Android
WebView with SiteIsolation disabled) cannot reuse or merge cached
UrlData entries and their origin-clean state across origins.

Fixed: 571058818
Change-Id: I8e17a3cb018a43137a3ca3ac4eae9ea756b17b87
Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8543392
Reviewed-by: Jordan Bayles <jophba@chromium.org>
Commit-Queue: Dale Curtis <dalecurtis@chromium.org>
Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1717208}

Electron adaptation notes (45-x-y): WebMediaPlayerImpl on 45-x-y still takes
a WebLocalFrame* instead of the (FrameScheduler*, security origin,
document URL, title, activation callback) parameter list that upstream had
refactored to before this fix, so the constructor signature is left as-is
and the new security_origin_ member is initialised from
frame_->GetSecurityOrigin() (WebSecurityOrigin converts to
scoped_refptr<const SecurityOrigin>). The DemuxerManager and media-log
origin arguments keep the branch's frame-based expressions. UrlIndex,
UrlData and the GetByUrl() call sites are unchanged from upstream.

